# What never needs to leave this laptop for a deploy.
#
# `vercel deploy` uploads the working directory, and it does not honour .gitignore the way git
# does — the first deploy carried 150 MB of model weights and ONNX runtime up to the build host,
# where the build then deleted them again. Worse, it carried this machine's
# `public/models/status.json`, which says the model IS installed, and the deployed app believed it.
#
# The build regenerates everything under public/ that it needs (see vercel.json's buildCommand).

node_modules
app/node_modules
app/dist
app/public/models
app/public/ort
app/public/sre
app/screenshots
app/test-results
app/playwright-report
.git
.vercel
